gnome-phone (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * neo-launcher: a default home screen. The first start takes
    neo-launcher/layout.json from /etc/xdg or /usr/share, and neo-launcher
    ships one: Phone, Contacts, Console and Messaging in the dock; Camera,
    Browser, Image Viewer, Calendar and Software on the first page; Document
    Viewer, Weather, Calculator and Settings on the second. An installed app
    it does not name goes where a fresh layout would put it (the phone's own
    apps on the first page, the others after); an app it names that is not
    installed leaves its cell empty. The clock and the compass stay in the
    drawer (hidden-from-home); the clock widget opens the clock.
  * gnome-phone-session: the dark style by default (color-scheme
    prefer-dark).

 -- pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0100

gnome-phone (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * extension: on Debian's GNOME Shell the screen shield already exports
    org.gnome.ScreenSaver; the extension's own export failed and the
    extension stopped half built (no keyboard, the screen going off every few
    seconds). The shell's object now steps aside while the extension runs.
  * neo-launcher: the first layout puts the phone's own apps on the first
    page and GNOME's and the rest from the second page on.
  * gnome-phone-session: GNOME's own screen lock off (lock-enabled=false).
    Locking too, it took the shell's unlock-dialog mode away under the
    extension's lock screen, and the right PIN left a black screen.

